    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.comment\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nThe `mini.comment` plugin has an `ignore_blank_line` option to skip blank lines when commenting, but this setting doesn't modify the definition of the \"comment\" textobject.\r\nFor example, when two paragraphs are commented out (e.g. after `gc2ap`), the comment block definition only covers the first paragraph and not the whole commented section.\r\n\r\nI feel like setting `ignore_blank_line` to true means that comment blocks also encompass blank lines, and IMHO the textobject should reflect this by skipping white lines. This behavior could either be the default or an additional plugin option.\r\nFor reference, this behavior is the default in tpope's vim-commentary.\r\n\r\nTo modify this behavior, I think a simple way would be to add a check for blank lines in the function returned by `H.make_comment_check` in the plugin:\r\n`return function(line) return H.is_blank(line) or string.find(line, regex) ~= nil end`\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.11.0\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Set the `ignore_blank_line` option to true\r\n2. Comment multiple paragraphs with `gc2ap`\r\n3. Execute an action on a comment block `dgc`\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nSkip the blank links in the definition of comment textobjects when `ignore_blank_line = true`\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nA comment textobject stops at the next blank line.",
    "closed_at": "2025-02-13T12:55:44Z",
