        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nAt first glance, this might be a reasonable behavior. Current behavior is documented as [matter only when commenting](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/690a3b4c78c4956f7ecf770124b522d32084b872/doc/mini-comment.txt#L80) and not when uncommenting or computing textobject range.\r\n\r\nAn actual implementation might be a bit tricky because I'd say that only blanks \"between\" commented blocks should be part of the textobject. I.e. uncommented ranges before first commented line and after last commented line should be used.\r\n\r\nI'll take a look, but I vaguely remember that textobject was not used affected by `config.ignore_blank_lines` for a reason.",
